y &= \sqrt{12^2+8^2} \\
P &= 4+12+\sqrt{80}+\sqrt{208} \\
P &\approx 39.37\text{ cm}
\end{align*}$$

Possibility 1: 18 cm and 22 cm are the shorter sides.
$$\begin{align*}
h &= \sqrt{18^2+22^2} \\
h &\approx 28.43\text{ cm}
\end{align*}$$
Possibility 2: 22 cm is the hypotenuse.
$$\begin{align*}
a &= \sqrt{22^2-18^2} \\
a &\approx 12.65\text{ cm}
\end{align*}$$

